{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:3c9033e5bbb23a5a8e333cef22364f98b0982688b433ec5e6b2f195dbb897bb6","grain":"paper-statement","id":"Entropy-and-Face-Dimension-of-the-Perfect-Matching-Polytope-September-23-2026#ex:lem-expansion-face","title":"The face of a triangle expansion"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/46b1e4e7c0f4a66421f57c89.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Lemma","generation_id":"sha256:fda4c3462963b650c538e2177794811eb1c221b267efea4b091fd6e397533f81","id":"r:Entropy-and-Face-Dimension-of-the-Perfect-Matching-Polytope-September-23-2026:ex:lem-expansion-face","kind":"statement-detail","manuscript_id":"p:Entropy-and-Face-Dimension-of-the-Perfect-Matching-Polytope-September-23-2026","name":"The face of a triangle expansion","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","printed_number":null,"printed_number_provenance":null,"printed_number_status":"unavailable","reading_page":"papers/Entropy-and-Face-Dimension-of-the-Perfect-Matching-Polytope-September-23-2026.html#ex:lem-expansion-face","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":5,"section_title":"Triangle expansions and sharp face codimension","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:9656fdba8f82bf49c4a1a0690cf982f5b37698311e86739fe092c1072edfb797","file":"preprints/Entropy-and-Face-Dimension-of-the-Perfect-Matching-Polytope-September-23-2026/build/sections/10-examples.tex","line":99,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":null,"provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Entropy-and-Face-Dimension-of-the-Perfect-Matching-Polytope-September-23-2026/build/sections/10-examples.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:9656fdba8f82bf49c4a1a0690cf982f5b37698311e86739fe092c1072edfb797","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Entropy-and-Face-Dimension-of-the-Perfect-Matching-Polytope-September-23-2026/build/sections/10-examples.tex#L99"},"statement_kind":"lemma","text":"\\label{ex:lem-expansion-face}\nThe set\n\\[\n Q_T=\\{y\\in P(G'):y(\\delta(T))=1\\}\n\\]\nis a face of \\(P(G')\\) affinely isomorphic to \\(P(G)\\). Under this\nisomorphism an old edge keeps its coordinate and\n\\[\n y_{f_i}=y_{e_i}\\qquad(1\\le i\\le3).\n\\]\nIf \\(x\\in P(G)\\) has coordinate \\(1/3\\) on every edge, its image\n\\(x'\\) has coordinate \\(1/3\\) on every edge of \\(G'\\).\nThe isomorphism maps the minimal face at \\(x\\) onto the minimal\nface at \\(x'\\)."}
